8 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095959 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "932f5592-30ac-5c62-b384-7f486827d8d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095960 #edb/ref 1080 "QT^(→) = a + c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095960 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095960 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "eb7de78d-2b15-5011-b093-b1ecd1d5d8f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095961 #edb/ref 1080 "QT^(→) = a + b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095961 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095961 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0100ff78-f852-53f3-b877-5a8f83dcffbe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095962 #edb/ref 1080 "QT^(→) = b + c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095962 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095962 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1c3729a5-b418-50e7-8211-78c4c9d786db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095963 #edb/ref 1080 "QT^(→) = b - c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095963 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095963 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "73d7f791-5754-5042-b83e-47ec093c5ba2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096444 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4277" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096444 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the diagram shown below, where $\\overrightarrow{PQ}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{c}.$ Find $\\overrightarrow{TS}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\mathbf{c}.$\n\n![](images/04/04ce04bf7c7f88d6578c74db0d7398a6d299d11bd9f60f4fc4b6e1bfb0129f3b.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096444 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e47a8da7-9276-5f4c-8ee6-1fd737c2e9ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096444 #edb/ref 1074 "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $S$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b,$ or $\\mathbf c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TP}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{PQ}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{QS}}}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/53/53940607b5cbf0220008e6e31ec60f2fd7fd2e4f70c5a8e95e7fcfd64064b095.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TP}} = -\\mathbf{b}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{PQ}} = \\mathbf{a}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{QS}} = \\mathbf{c}.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](images/81/810cce10eb330b1767a101d9107a9534c437daa123f13056a486a9fc96dbab89.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TS} & =\\overset{\\to }{TP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QS} \\\\  & =-b+a+c \\\\  & =a-b+c.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096486 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5015" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096486 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/24/2420154d44b786c6aad54212760e9a37ce67dbdce94a7043039f0e824c5ef9bc.png)\n\nIn parallelogram $ABCD$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{CB}+\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{CA}$\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{CB}-\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\overrightarrow{AC}$\n\n- $\\overrightarrow{DC}=\\overrightarrow{BA}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096486 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0b0dbbc1-d39d-5aff-9f16-075779d36659" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096486 #edb/ref 1074 "- Equality I is true. Indeed, $\\overrightarrow{CB}+\\overrightarrow{BA}=\\overrightarrow{CA}.$\n\n- Equality II is false. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CB}-\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BA} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CA} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{AC}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nsince $\\overrightarrow{CA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ have opposite directions.\n\n- Equality III is false. Indeed, $\\overrightarrow{DC}\\neq\\overrightarrow{BA}$ since they have opposite directions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096603 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9934" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096603 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/74/7431bd3281e4e49f4caaa5b701885fb64c58196b2256af9d8744decd9a0d0793.png)\n\n  \n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overrightarrow{PS}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overrightarrow{QS}=\\mathbf{b},$ $\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\mathbf{c},$ and $\\overrightarrow{TS}=\\mathbf{d}.$ Find $\\overrightarrow{TQ}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b}, \\mathbf{c},$ and $\\mathbf{d}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096603 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c7526e18-37a9-572a-a6a3-0384bbccf41d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096603 #edb/ref 1074 "We want to find a \"path\" from $T$ to $Q$ consisting only of the vectors $\\mathbf a, \\mathbf b, \\mathbf c,$ and $\\mathbf d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition, \n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{\\overrightarrow{TQ}}} = {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{TS}}} + {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/49/4902397acd28e2e5f85063ba55c576d3768360225a705f31a66bd460405dd5a6.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\overrightarrow{TS}} = \\mathbf{d}, \\qquad {\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{SQ}}} = -\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](images/08/08086f7e09568f908aa4919a1156d52e465216221be8908e72a1fd90ec8843dd.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{TS}+\\overset{\\to }{SQ} \\\\  & =d+(-b) \\\\  & =d-b.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096647 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097027 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096647 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096647 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186235510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096647 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272290 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096647 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272386 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096647 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186275087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096647 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294891 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096647 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186302396 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096647 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096647 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096647 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096647 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186388834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096647 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186388869 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096647 #edb/ref 1039 "Expressing a Vector as a Sum or Difference of More Than Two Known Vectors" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096647 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186096444 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096647 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "33f0ec6b-9cb4-5246-9ac6-23b35e3b224e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096691 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097175 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096691 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097340 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096691 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096691 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186275088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096691 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186275089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096691 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186335981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096691 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345292 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096691 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Vector Equalities" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096691 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186096486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096691 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "c015dcaa-2155-5d80-985b-21924de92b28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096794 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186096960 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097339 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247336 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272334 #edb/ref 17592186045417] 