(→) = c$. Find $QT^(→)$ in terms of $a, b$, and $c$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097027 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "eceb91e0-95b6-5672-af4d-3210bb9c13a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097339 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186095958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097339 #edb/ref 1069 "q-69532" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097339 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/51/511855eb6fdfc8f7766017a4fb458a0351a44e33e78db94f3cc3442469f023a6.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $PS^(→) = a$, $QP^(→) = b$, and $PT^(→) = c$. Find $QT^(→)$ in terms of $a, b$, and $c$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097339 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7d3516c8-28b0-5e4b-9932-941d12dfb35d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097476 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097709 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097476 #edb/ref 1061 15694 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097476 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "60458875-ac64-5849-86d5-1d54ffdf12af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097476 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097831 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097477 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097548 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097477 #edb/ref 1061 15695 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097477 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7edff0ab-8d12-5173-baab-3ba46883ba4d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097477 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097548 #edb/ref 1061 18415 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097548 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3c69fb77-271a-5dcc-af1c-f2f7b0d14282" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097548 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096691 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097709 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097709 #edb/ref 1061 37408 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097709 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1d59ceb2-63e4-5d77-913c-73dbfc0ece9e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097709 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097831 #edb/ref 1064 "It's often helpful to express a given vector in terms of sums and scalar multiples of a handful of known vectors.\n\nAs an example, let's consider the following diagram:\n\n![](images/a6/a6c8dcdf9be32345bbc92ff162992e6c9cf02c107de8ff74caf534b508bfe411.png)\n\nHow can we express the vector $\\overrightarrow{PR}$ in terms of the vectors $\\textbf{a}$ and $\\textbf{b}$ only?\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PR} & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QR}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/8c/8c72ba23124e9622b50f9daee4006ca4aac6a460b8a694a368d0e53393a85053.png)\n\nFrom the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{PQ}}}   = \\mathbf{a} \\qquad\\textrm{and}\\qquad\n{\\color{blue}{\\overrightarrow{QR}}}  = -\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\n![](images/9d/9d284b2d2683ae43fe57e8c96433803bc908d764e489ac0f861ad978393fde7d.png)\n\nTherefore, by substituting these values into our equation for ${\\color{red}\\overrightarrow{PR}},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PR} & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QR} \\\\  & =\\text{a}+(-\\text{b}) \\\\  & =\\text{a}-\\text{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's see another example." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097831 #edb/ref 1065 2904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097831 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "d92705a2-c9e5-5782-91e1-fa086fa5bffb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097831 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244796 #edb/ref 1080 "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=d-a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244796 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244796 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "367788ba-9c7c-5e7c-8d21-94b3c4ba0009" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245562 #edb/ref 1080 "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=c-a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245562 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245562 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8f148817-c745-530a-a8b8-28d7b5e4345e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245918 #edb/ref 1080 "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=a-b-c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245918 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245918 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b417d004-817e-5033-a8fd-22b425d08539" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245957 #edb/ref 1080 "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=a+b-c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245957 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245957 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b7e4a15b-18c4-5947-9ba2-a025c8d4e9c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246504 #edb/ref 1080 "\\overset{\\to }{XW}=d+a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246504 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246504 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f8bce547-b8ee-520e-ad41-e9f53f4bdc96" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246917 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186244796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246917 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186245562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246917 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186245918 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246917 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186245957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246917 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186246504 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246917 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246917 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246917 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186244796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246917 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cdcf588e-a428-59ae-a4f9-9b453b8f13ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247336 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246917 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247336 #edb/ref 1069 "q-11323" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247336 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247336 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/36/36aaf58af536428c74cdb8f4c02c2b4f07e414422e8aea378c75d7abcff58cff.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{YX}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{XV}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{VZ}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{YW}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{XW}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247336 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4193f1f9-5dd6-5e42-ab53-c9d471fede26" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247336 #edb/ref 1074 "We want to find a \"path\" from $X$ to $W$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$  \n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{XW}=\\overset{\\to }{XY}+\\overset{\\to }{YW},\n$$\n\nas shown below. \n\n![](images/47/4758b51fd3dc076059d60e944de0ad8375bb304240365959d4c6cae94f95a535.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{XY}=-a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{YW}=d.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](images/e9/e942d61c1f51c36dc6cd04f88ff5e37f538920a34c1af5bc780c47691567b668.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{XW} & =\\overset{\\to }{XY}+\\overset{\\to }{YW} \\\\  & =-a+d \\\\  & =d-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387008 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186387009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387008 #edb/ref 1069 "q-12049" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387008 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387008 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/2f/2f9e6eff196e24ddabca8d778d27e499fc1b856ef7169257a31a7cbaca8b564b.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{TP}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{TS}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RS}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{QT}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387008 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b958283a-525c-51ab-a33e-68049ee3df0d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387008 #edb/ref 1074 "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $T$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QT}=\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PT},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/e1/e1d5eb2f392332f69fa1507899b30b838a42ebd1c40dacddeca4edcf0f7aa8c2.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PT}=-b.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](images/0e/0e8e24968141284550fac7d4e5c63333789f30ade8f7d5dd8b87fae4e012673a.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QT} & =\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PT} \\\\  & =a+(-b) \\\\  & =a-b\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387009 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387009 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387009 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387012 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387009 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387009 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387009 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387009 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387009 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186387012 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387009 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "80e3c074-2fe2-56ad-8be9-99fa6a58e9b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387010 #edb/ref 1080 "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=b-c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387010 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387010 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "60fa9802-8c91-55e9-84a5-e1363e2e7308" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387011 #edb/ref 1080 "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=b+c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387011 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387011 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9d30e4cd-7866-5dc8-9d17-e3603b0e1d04" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387012 #edb/ref 1080 "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=a-b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387012 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387012 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0e6b1f27-9577-571f-a402-5318532c66a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387013 #edb/ref 1080 "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=a+b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387013 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417